Counting precision depends on exposure and the event model (@cm-count-statistics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/CPC-Proportionality-Calibration-Owen-Mulholland-Guthrie.lingua#r_7XKKJ1Q7HNDS2BEPSHZDJMTKVE", #clean-manufacturing "A-zero-count-constrains-a-model-rather-than-proving-absence.lingua#r_2DHX4M9DNKZ1WSD6FFKQHHKTQA") { r_2JFR35FEQVGGN8XZAH4J885ZJH
**Read:** [CPC proportionality calibration — Owen, Mulholland and Guthrie](../sources/CPC-Proportionality-Calibration-Owen-Mulholland-Guthrie.lingua#r_7XKKJ1Q7HNDS2BEPSHZDJMTKVE), dilution observations and counting uncertainty. Use [Sampling contributions, thresholds, and results near zero](../../../inquiry/metrology/uncertainty/Sampling-and-censoring.lingua#r_3RRJRMNNAPMVYJ9Z6VGY2DV0CG) to connect a sample to the population of interest.

For independent events arriving at a constant rate with no unresolved counting loss, N follows a Poisson distribution with mean λ = CEV, where V is sampled volume and E is a known overall detection/transfer factor. Var(N) = λ. The estimator Ĉ = N/(EV) has variance C/(EV); substituting N gives an approximate counting standard uncertainty √N/(EV) when that approximation is useful.

The relative counting uncertainty is approximately 1/√N. At N = 100 it is 10%; at N = 10000 it is 1%. Four times the exposure halves this counting contribution under the same model. It does not halve an unknown efficiency bias or variation between unobserved locations.

For V = 10 L, E = 0.8 and N = 64, Ĉ = 8 L⁻¹ and the estimated counting standard uncertainty is 1 L⁻¹. Calibration and sampling-model contributions remain to be added. Low counts need an appropriate asymmetric interval rather than an automatically symmetric normal interval extending below zero.

**Work:** Derive the Poisson mean and variance from independent rare events or a probability-generating function. Compare a constant-rate model with clustered releases or a changing rate. Use replicate time windows to investigate variability without interpreting every departure from Poisson behavior as an instrument failure. Keep raw counts distinct from corrected concentrations and rounded displays.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
